/**
 * Delete junction rows for commits that are no longer reachable from any
 * branch. Used after branch deletion or force-push.
 *
 * Reachability is checked against `repo_branch_commits` rather than
 * `cc.branch`. Callers run `deleteRepoBranchCommitsByBranch` first, so by
 * the time this query runs the deleted/force-pushed branch is already gone
 * from `repo_branch_commits`. The `NOT EXISTS` then drops only commits
 * that were exclusively on that branch — junctions for commits still
 * living on another branch survive, even if their `cc.branch` field
 * happens to record the now-deleted one (per-branch fanout in the upsert
 * path made that possible).
 *
 * The `branch` parameter is retained for callers and metrics but is no
 * longer used for filtering — `cc.branch` is not the source of truth for
 * reachability. After deletion, `deleteOrphanedCheckpoints` should be
 * called to clean up checkpoint metadata that lost all junctions.
